Station: BMGS-bori-field, Bori Metropolis.

The interpreted subsurface model consists of six layers. The resistivity sequence starts at 1005 $\Omega$m, rises to 3588 $\Omega$m (Layer 2), and then decreases through Layer 3 (1358 $\Omega$m) and Layer 4 (333 $\Omega$m). The sequence concludes with a significant increase through Layer 5 (2950 $\Omega$m) and Layer 6 (5469 $\Omega$m). Applying the vertical electrical sounding (VES) notation, this profile results in a KQHA-type curve. This classification is consistent with the survey interpretation currently on file.

